IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ma-types`

-- Metrication Act 1970 (Singapore) — ss 1-7 and the four Schedules, the
-- whole Act.
--
-- Source: ../source/MA1970.txt lines 54-231 (SSO PDF, current version as at
-- 05 Oct 2026, 2020 Revised Edition; the 1985 edition's Schedules A-D are
-- now the First to Fourth Schedules). s 6 lets the Minister vary the
-- Schedules by Gazette notification; the Schedules here are as printed, and
-- a later notification would be a new version this encoding does not have.

§ `Metrication Act 1970`

§§ `Long title, and 1. Short title`

-- INERT. "An Act to introduce the use of the International System of Units
-- in Singapore, to enable necessary modifications of legislation to be
-- effected and for matters connected therewith." [15 February 1971]
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1 — short title` MEANS "This Act is the Metrication Act 1970."

§§ `The Schedules, as data`

-- First, Second and Fourth Schedules: "Unit, Symbol, Quantity", each row
-- copied from the source. A unit no Schedule lists answers NOTHING: that is a
-- lookup that misses, not an outcome.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 First, Second and Fourth Schedules
GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE `Unit row`
`the Schedule row for` u MEANS
    CONSIDER u
    --                                          schedule                symbol  quantity
    WHEN metre       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "m",    "length")
    WHEN kilogram    THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "kg",   "mass")
    WHEN second      THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "s",    "time")
    WHEN ampere      THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "A",    "electric current")
    WHEN kelvin      THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "K",    "thermodynamic temperature")
    WHEN candela     THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`,  "cd",   "luminous intensity")
    WHEN hertz       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Hz",   "frequency")
    WHEN newton      THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "N",    "force")
    WHEN joule       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "J",    "work, energy, quantity of heat")
    WHEN watt        THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "W",    "power")
    WHEN coulomb     THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "C",    "quantity of electricity, electric charge")
    WHEN volt        THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "V",    "electric tension, potential difference, electromotive force")
    WHEN farad       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "F",    "electric capacitance")
    WHEN ohm         THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Ω",    "electric resistance")
    WHEN weber       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Wb",   "flux of magnetic induction, magnetic flux")
    WHEN tesla       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "T",    "magnetic flux density, magnetic induction")
    WHEN henry       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "H",    "inductance")
    WHEN lumen       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "lm",   "luminous flux")
    WHEN lux         THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "lx",   "illumination")
    WHEN radian      THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "rad",  "plane angle")
    WHEN steradian   THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "sr",   "solid angle")
    WHEN hectare     THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "ha",   "area")
    WHEN `metric tonne` THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "t", "mass")
    WHEN litre       THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "L",    "volume")
    WHEN `centigrade or Celsius` THEN JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "°C", "temperature, temperature interval")
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Third Schedule: "Conversion of Imperial Standard Units to Equivalent SI
-- Units" and "Conversion of Local Customary Units to Equivalent SI Units".
-- The gallon is printed twice, "= 4.54609 litres approximately" and
-- "= 4.54609 cubic decimetres approximately"; one row carries both.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 Third Schedule
GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A MAYBE Conversion
`the Third Schedule conversion for` u MEANS
    CONSIDER u
    --                                     SI value     SI unit                          exactly
    WHEN yard   THEN JUST (Conversion OF 0.9144,     "metre",                         TRUE)
    WHEN pound  THEN JUST (Conversion OF 0.45359237, "kilogram",                      TRUE)
    WHEN gallon THEN JUST (Conversion OF 4.54609,    "litres (= cubic decimetres)",   FALSE)
    WHEN tahil  THEN JUST (Conversion OF 37.799364,  "grams",                         FALSE)
    WHEN kati   THEN JUST (Conversion OF 0.604790,   "kilogram",                      FALSE)
    WHEN chhun  THEN JUST (Conversion OF 37.465,     "millimetres",                   TRUE)
    WHEN chhek  THEN JUST (Conversion OF 0.37465,    "metre",                         TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 5(a), (b); Third Schedule headings
GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A `System of the unit`
`the system of` u MEANS
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN yard   THEN `an imperial standard of extension, weight or capacity`
    WHEN pound  THEN `an imperial standard of extension, weight or capacity`
    WHEN gallon THEN `an imperial standard of extension, weight or capacity`
    WHEN tahil  THEN `the local customary system of weights and measures`
    WHEN kati   THEN `the local customary system of weights and measures`
    WHEN chhun  THEN `the local customary system of weights and measures`
    WHEN chhek  THEN `the local customary system of weights and measures`
    OTHERWISE `neither`

§§ `2. Interpretation, and 3. International System of Units`

-- s 2(1): "'International System of Units' — (a) means the metric system of
-- units as set out in the First and Second Schedules; and (b) includes the
-- units set out in the Fourth Schedule unless there is something in the
-- subject or context thereof inconsistent with such construction or unless
-- it is therein otherwise expressly provided." s 3(2) lists the same three.
-- Whether a written law's subject or context excludes the Fourth Schedule
-- units is a reading of that law: an input.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 ss 2(1), 3(2)
GIVEN u                                 IS A Unit
      `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST row THEN CONSIDER row's `schedule`
                       WHEN `the First Schedule`  THEN TRUE                                               -- (a), s 3(2)(a)
                       WHEN `the Second Schedule` THEN TRUE                                               -- (a), s 3(2)(b)
                       WHEN `the Fourth Schedule` THEN NOT `the context excludes the Fourth Schedule`      -- (b), s 3(2)(c)
                       OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2(2): "The abbreviation 'SI' is recognised as a legal reference to the
-- International System of Units."
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 2(2)
GIVEN abbreviation IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a recognised legal reference to the International System of Units:` abbreviation IF
    abbreviation EQUALS "SI"

-- s 3(1): "On and after 15 February 1971, the use of the system of units
-- known as the International System of Units has legal force and validity in
-- Singapore." Before that day this Act gives it none — the Act's own answer.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 3(1)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` d IF
    d AT LEAST YMD 1971 2 15

§§ `4. Power to adapt, etc.`

-- s 4(1): the Minister "may by order provide for the adaptation, alteration,
-- conversion or modification of any provisions contained in any written law
-- ... for the purpose of replacing references to units other than metric
-- units ... with references to units of the International System of Units
-- which are either — (a) equivalent; or (b) such approximations as appear to
-- the Minister desirable ...". s 4(2): "Any order made under subsection (1)
-- must be published in the Gazette."
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 4
GIVEN o IS A `Section 4 order`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order within s 4` o IF
        "(1)" ... o's `replaces references to non-metric units in written law with SI units`
    AND "(1)(a) or (b)" ... o's `each replacement is equivalent or a desirable approximation`
    AND "(2)" ... o's `published in the Gazette`

§§ `5. Conversion of imperial standard units to metric system units`

-- s 5: "The values expressed in terms of — (a) any imperial standard relating
-- to measures of extension whether lineal, superficial or solid, or of weight
-- or capacity; or (b) the local customary system of weights and measures, may
-- be converted into the values expressed in terms of the International System
-- of Units in accordance with the Third Schedule."
-- A permission ("may be converted"); the figure is what the Schedule gives.
-- A unit the Third Schedule does not list has no conversion under s 5.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 5; Third Schedule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A Unit
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the SI value of` n u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule conversion for` u
    WHEN JUST c  THEN n TIMES c's `SI value of one unit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the Third Schedule gives no conversion for this unit"

§§ `6. Power to vary Schedules`

-- s 6: "The Minister may, from time to time by notification in the Gazette,
-- add to, vary or amend the Schedules as the Minister may think fit." INERT:
-- a power; the Schedules above are as printed on 05 Oct 2026. (The PDF's text
-- layer displaces the word "Gazette"; see ../source/PROVENANCE.md.)

§§ `7. Saving`

-- s 7(1): "No act or thing done before the making of any order under section 4
-- may be challenged only on the ground that the act or thing done was done in
-- a unit other than a unit of the International System of Units."
--
-- FORK F1: "before the making of any order under section 4" is read as
-- before the order that touches the act in question — the order that
-- converted the written law under which it was done. The other reading,
-- before the first s 4 order of any kind, would fix one date for every law.
-- The input is that order's date, or NOTHING if no such order has been made.
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 7(1)
GIVEN `done on`               IS A DATE
      `the order was made on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `challenged only on the units ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(1) bars a challenge to an act done on` `done on` `, the order made on` `the order was made on` `, on the units ground only:` `challenged only on the units ground` IF
        `challenged only on the units ground`
    AND CONSIDER `the order was made on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE                       -- every act is before an order not yet made
        WHEN JUST o  THEN `done on` LESS THAN o

-- s 7(2): "Nothing in this Act affects the legal force and validity of any
-- other system of units lawfully used in Singapore."
@ref Metrication Act 1970 s 7(2)
GIVEN `lawfully used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act leaves another system's legal force untouched, it being lawfully used:` `lawfully used in Singapore` IF
    `lawfully used in Singapore`
